/target

# The fuzz crate builds into its own target dir.
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/Cargo.lock

# Crashing inputs found by a run. These are evidence, not source: when a run
# finds one, minimize it and turn it into a regression test rather than
# committing the raw artifact.
/fuzz/artifacts

# Coverage reports from `make fuzz-coverage`.
/fuzz/coverage

# libFuzzer grows the corpus as it explores. The hand-written seeds under
# fuzz/corpus/<target>/ ARE committed — they are what gets a fuzzer past the
# magic number and into the parser on a cold start — but a machine-grown
# corpus is large, uninteresting to read, and regenerable, so it stays out.
# Seeds are named seed-*; everything else libFuzzer writes is ignored.
/fuzz/corpus/*/*
!/fuzz/corpus/*/seed-*
